esc-kaunas-artists-house-living-kaunas-2.about:
Kaunas Artists’ House brings fresh and unexpected cultural experiences, connecting local and international communities, and promoting openness and inclusion through culture. Kaunas Artists’ House is always on the lookout for new ideas, young artists, and diverse audiences through artist residencies, cultural education programs, and community events. Tasks: Assisting in and leading educational activities with different groups of teenagers; Preparing for events and helping to maintain the place: organizing the venue, creating the physical atmosphere, greeting guests; Distributing promotional material and promoting our work to foreigners living in Kaunas; Organizing parts of big events together with local volunteers; Doing your own project according to our organization's values and standards;

Practical details: Individual European Solidarity Corps volunteering hosted by Kauno menininkų namai in Kaunas, Lithuania; activity period up to 13 months (15 March 2026 – 15 April 2027). Topics: culture and creativity. Residents of Georgia are explicitly accepted, together with 29 other countries. Applications are rolling, so apply early.

Living and learning: Accommodation in a private room in a shared apartment Monthly ticket for public transport Monthly food and pocket money On-arrival and mid-term trainings Monthly volunteer group meetings and meetings with a mentor Online Lithuanian language classes Organization of solidarity and volunteering events As in every ESC project, accommodation, food, local transport, insurance and pocket money are covered, travel is reimbursed by distance band, and volunteers get training, a mentor, language support and a Youthpass certificate.
